Q. Why is an Ingress Controller classified as a "Layer 7" Load Balancer, whereas a standard Kubernetes Service (LoadBalancer type) is "Layer 4"?
Ans. Ingress routes traffic based on HTTP Headers (Host) and URL Paths, while Services route based only on IP and Port.

Q11. Host-Based Routing Logic
Solved
In a scenario where multiple domains (e.g., api.company.com and admin.company.com) resolve to the same Ingress IP address, how does the Ingress Controller determine which Service to send the traffic to?
Ans. It inspects the Host HTTP header in the incoming request.

Q2. Path Matching Mechanics
Solved
You have configured an Ingress with paths /blue and /green. If you set pathType: Prefix for the /blue path, which of the following requests would match that rule?
Ans. /blue and /blue/whales.
Prefix means the request path must start with /blue as a complete path element. It matches /blue and any subpaths under it.
✅ Matches:
/blue
/blue/
/blue/app
/blue/v1/test
❌ Does NOT match:
/blu
/bluegreen
/green

